An item that holds a checkbox and no text survives, and keeps its sublist.

A checkbox is state, so a box on its own IS content. Dropping the item as
empty lost the box outright, and did worse than that when the item held a
nested list: the parent vanished and its child was left at four leading
spaces, which reads back as an indented code block rather than a list, so
the whole list was destroyed and the output no longer settled.

The trailing space after the box is deliberate. `- [ ]` with nothing after
it is not a task item to cmark, so the space is what lets an empty box come
back as a box.
